[SO-64507986] Q: Method not found: 'setState' even though I'm in a Stateful Widget
A: <p>Christopher's answer tells you how to fix the problem, but what the problem actually was is that you are calling <code>setState</code> within the initializer for the <code>_widgetOptions</code> class field. You cannot use any of the class's members within an initializer in that class that is not marked <code>static</code> or otherwise accessible from a static context (i.e. without calling <code>this</code> either explicitly or implicitly). Since <code>setState</code> is an instance method and must be accessed by (implicitly) calling <code>this</code>, it doesn't yet exist when <code>_widgetOptions</code> is getting initialized.</p>
<p>Take the following, for example:</p>
<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>class Foo {
  // An instance method that does not exist until the constructor is called
  // and all instance initializers have run
  int a() { return 2; }

  // A static method that is created at the same time as the class type itself 
  // and exists before any constructors and instance initializers have run
  static int b() { return 3; }

  // This is fine
 int x = b();

  // This is also fine
  int y;
  void doSomething() {
    y = a();
  }

  // This will throw an error because `this` does not yet exist when `z` 
  // gets initialized and calling `a()` implicitly becomes `this.a()`
  int z = a();
}
</code></pre>
<p>Moving the initializer to within the <code>build</code> method or converting it to a method itself as Christopher suggests will solve the issue.</p>


