<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;body&gt;
&lt;button type="button" id="button1" onclick="foo()"&gt;Result!&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;script type="text/javascript"&gt;
  function foo() {
    var button = document.getElementById("button1");
    button.innerText = "&lt;strong&gt;my text&lt;/strong&gt;"
  }
  &lt;/script&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

<p><strong>Note:</strong> Firefox doesn't support innerText, but has its own property called <strong>textContent</strong>, which can be used instead.</p>


