[SO-40231106] Q: Dynamically edit a link to change video source
A: <p>Here is what worked for me thanks to @Tushar</p>

<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$('#button').on({
    'click': function(){
    var inputvalue = $("#input").val();
    $('#videot').attr('src', "http://example.com/episode/" + inputvalue + "/something.mp4");
    }
});</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;
&lt;input type="text" value="Episode Number" id="input"&gt;
&lt;button type="button" class='btn' id="button"&gt;Watch&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;video id='videot' width="100%" controls="controls"&gt;
&lt;source src="http://example.com/episode/25/something.mp4" type="video/mp4"&gt;
Your browser does not support this video's playback.&lt;/video&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>


[SO-23148292] Q: Javascript function change content onclick
A: <p>No need for <code>.</code> after <code>getElementById</code></p>

<pre><code>&lt;script language="javascript" type="text/javascript"&gt;
 function changeText(idElement) {
    if(idElement==1){
        document.getElementById('tagmain').innerHTML ='New title to display';
        document.getElementById('tagtext').innerHTML ='New text to display.'; // removed extra }
        return false;
    }
 }
 &lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>HTML changes</p>

<pre><code>&lt;div class="banner_button"&gt;
   &lt;a id="support" href="#" onclick="javascript:changeText(1); return false;"&gt;Support&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>OR you can use jQuery to set html </p>

<pre><code>&lt;script language="javascript" type="text/javascript"&gt;
 function changeText(idElement) {
    if(idElement==1){
        $('#tagmain').html('New title to display');
        $('#tagtext').html('New text to display.');
        return false;
    }
 }
 &lt;/script&gt;
</code></pre>


